From a9a9cd94d3a4b4284f9afb7fb9b79eadd79c311e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: architecture review <review@local>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 13:01:52 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] T4 prototype: knowledge records in the ADR-0011 history
 manifest (ADR-0013 draft)

Review branch from dcd43f1, built by the independent architecture review
after the designer approved ADR-0013 with terminology edits. Not for merge
as is; it gives the M6b plan something concrete to diff against.

- history.schema.json: entry kinds reference, case, lesson, disposition,
  receipt; optional integer `version`.
- control.schema.json: a v2-only `knowledge` block (capture cursor, bounded
  pending list, overflow count), forbidden on v1 like the other v2 keys.
- Record schemas aew/knowledge/{case,disposition,receipt}/v1.
- history/store.py: knowledge record paths under .aew/knowledge/, covered by
  RECORD_GLOBS so the orphan check and the audit see them.
- history/index.py: about(), versions(), current() with the disposition
  fold, an FTS5 table over knowledge bodies and search(); every hit is
  authenticated at its position (locator, not voucher).
- engine/knowledge_ops.py and cli/knowledge_commands.py: `aew knowledge
  case|dispose|show|list|search`; one Lead transaction writes case,
  initial disposition and receipt through History.write_record and
  ctx.entries; the full audit appends the knowledge link checks.
- tools/perf/control_plane.py: the v1 fixture drops the knowledge block as
  it drops `cold`.
- tests: invariants rule 29 (a disposition's subject precedes it);
  test_knowledge_manifest.py (8) and test_knowledge_surface.py (6).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
